Z||000000||Jncomutt||05-12-2001||05:27 PM||||Ok, I did a search on ebrake topics and nothing seemed to address my problem.<P>I put my car up on jackstands, turn the wheel, and pushed the brake pedal, and the tires stop spinning.  So I know that the hydrolic components of my calipers work.  When I pull up the e-brake handle, however, tires keep spinning.<P>I adjusted the equalizer bolt as far as it will go and still no affect.  I know all the cables are hooked up ok because I can see the the spring compress and the lever on the caliper being pulled.<P>Someone told me I should try to adjust the bolt on the caliper itself.  When I tried to do this, it backed out til it stopped.  So I tried turnin the nut the other way but the bolt itself went into the caliper so I couldn't get a wrench on it.  I undid it so that the lever would fit back on and put it back together.  Is that adjusting nut supposed to move in and out?  If not, what do I check for? I heard the "sliding pins?" could be stuck, not really too sure, I didn't look into that yet.  I knew I'd be able to hopefully get some advice here before I tried.  Anyhelp would be appreciated, thanks again. ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Hardworker||05-12-2001||06:57 PM||||It sounds like the oneway clutch is frozen in the brake caliber.  First remove the ecable from the arm on the caliber.  Then ratchet the arm back an forth until the rotor cannot be turned by hand when the arm on the caliber is forward. If it don't work like above then the ebrake is frozen inside the caliber and will require disassembly to repair.||||reg||1
